nges during early life, influenced by factors such as the method of birth and dietary intake.\n\nOverall, the intestinal microbiota is essential for energy homeostasis and has profound implications for human health, particularly in relation to metabolic conditions.", "HYPERPHENYLALANINEMIA:Hyperphenylalaninemia is a clinical condition characterized by elevated levels of phenylalanine in the blood, often due to a metabolic defect.", "AMINOÁCIDOS EXENTOS DE FENILALANINA:Commercial preparations of amino acids free of phenylalanine are used for supplementation in patients with phenylketonuria."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}